IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `mc97-nouns`
IMPORT `mc97-saving`

-- TESTS for mc97-saving.l4. Every expected value is written from the text of the three unnumbered paragraphs
-- (extract lines 41, 44 and 47), before the run. Traces carry an `-- expect:` line that check-traces.py reads back.

§ `Tests: the General Saving`

§§ `First paragraph: the reservation ("Reserving to all Archbishops, Bishops, ... and all Persons")`

-- Named in the list: Archbishops, Bishops, Abbots, Priors, Templars, Hospitallers, Earls, Barons. The rest are reached as "all Persons".
#ASSERT `first paragraph: how the reservation reaches` `an Archbishop` EQUALS `named in the list`
#ASSERT `first paragraph: how the reservation reaches` `a Bishop` EQUALS `named in the list`
#ASSERT `first paragraph: how the reservation reaches` `an Abbot` EQUALS `named in the list`
#ASSERT `first paragraph: how the reservation reaches` `a Prior` EQUALS `named in the list`
#ASSERT `first paragraph: how the reservation reaches` `an Earl` EQUALS `named in the list`
#ASSERT `first paragraph: how the reservation reaches` `a Baron` EQUALS `named in the list`
#ASSERT `first paragraph: how the reservation reaches` `a Freeman of the Realm` EQUALS `reached as one of all Persons`
#ASSERT `first paragraph: how the reservation reaches` `a Templar` EQUALS `named in the list`
#ASSERT `first paragraph: how the reservation reaches` `a Hospitaller` EQUALS `named in the list`
#ASSERT `first paragraph: how the reservation reaches` `a Knight` EQUALS `reached as one of all Persons`
#ASSERT `first paragraph: how the reservation reaches` `a Freeholder` EQUALS `reached as one of all Persons`
#ASSERT `first paragraph: how the reservation reaches` `another Subject` EQUALS `reached as one of all Persons`
#ASSERT `first paragraph: how the reservation reaches` `another Person` EQUALS `reached as one of all Persons`

-- What is reserved: their free Liberties and free Customs, which they have had in time passed. Both limbs are needed.
-- Arguments: the Liberty or Custom is free; they have had it in time passed.
#ASSERT `first paragraph: the reservation reserves` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `covered by the text`
#ASSERT `first paragraph: the reservation reserves` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `not covered by the text`
#ASSERT `first paragraph: the reservation reserves` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `not covered by the text`
#ASSERT `first paragraph: the reservation reserves` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not covered by the text`

§§ `First paragraph: "we shall observe"; "all Men of this our Realm ... shall observe"`

-- Arguments: it is one of the Customs and Liberties aforesaid; it appertaineth to the King and his Heirs.
#ASSERT `first paragraph: the King shall observe` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `covered by the text`
#ASSERT `first paragraph: the King shall observe` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `not covered by the text`
#ASSERT `first paragraph: the King shall observe` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `not covered by the text`
#ASSERT `first paragraph: the King shall observe` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not covered by the text`
-- Arguments: the person is a Man of this our Realm; observing lies within his power ("as much as in them is").
#ASSERT `first paragraph: a Man of the Realm shall observe` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `covered by the text`
#ASSERT `first paragraph: a Man of the Realm shall observe` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `not covered by the text`
#ASSERT `first paragraph: a Man of the Realm shall observe` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `not covered by the text`
#ASSERT `first paragraph: a Man of the Realm shall observe` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not covered by the text`

-- expect: FULFILLED
#TRACE `first paragraph: the King shall observe the Customs and Liberties` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the King` DOES `observe the Customs and Liberties` AT 5
-- No time limit is stated: with nothing done, the duty stands.
-- expect: STANDING
#TRACE `first paragraph: the King shall observe the Customs and Liberties` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 100000)
-- expect: FULFILLED
#TRACE `first paragraph: a Man of the Realm shall observe the Customs and Liberties` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a Man of the Realm` DOES `observe the Customs and Liberties` AT 5
-- expect: STANDING
#TRACE `first paragraph: a Man of the Realm shall observe the Customs and Liberties` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 100000)

§§ `First paragraph: the subsidy ("have given unto Us the Fifteenth Part of all their Moveables")`

-- Who gave: Archbishops, Bishops, Abbots, Priors, Earls, Barons, Knights, Freeholders, and other Subjects. Nine; the rest are not named.
#ASSERT `first paragraph: the Fifteenth Part of Moveables was given by` `an Archbishop` EQUALS `covered by the text`
#ASSERT `first paragraph: the Fifteenth Part of Moveables was given by` `a Bishop` EQUALS `covered by the text`
#ASSERT `first paragraph: the Fifteenth Part of Moveables was given by` `an Abbot` EQUALS `covered by the text`
#ASSERT `first paragraph: the Fifteenth Part of Moveables was given by` `a Prior` EQUALS `covered by the text`
#ASSERT `first paragraph: the Fifteenth Part of Moveables was given by` `an Earl` EQUALS `covered by the text`
#ASSERT `first paragraph: the Fifteenth Part of Moveables was given by` `a Baron` EQUALS `covered by the text`
#ASSERT `first paragraph: the Fifteenth Part of Moveables was given by` `a Freeman of the Realm` EQUALS `not covered by the text`
#ASSERT `first paragraph: the Fifteenth Part of Moveables was given by` `a Templar` EQUALS `not covered by the text`
#ASSERT `first paragraph: the Fifteenth Part of Moveables was given by` `a Hospitaller` EQUALS `not covered by the text`
#ASSERT `first paragraph: the Fifteenth Part of Moveables was given by` `a Knight` EQUALS `covered by the text`
#ASSERT `first paragraph: the Fifteenth Part of Moveables was given by` `a Freeholder` EQUALS `covered by the text`
#ASSERT `first paragraph: the Fifteenth Part of Moveables was given by` `another Subject` EQUALS `covered by the text`
#ASSERT `first paragraph: the Fifteenth Part of Moveables was given by` `another Person` EQUALS `not covered by the text`
-- The Fifteenth Part is one fifteenth.
#ASSERT `first paragraph: the Fifteenth Part of` 1500 EQUALS 100
#ASSERT `first paragraph: the Fifteenth Part of` 15 EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `first paragraph: the Fifteenth Part of` 30 EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `first paragraph: the Fifteenth Part of` 0 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT (`first paragraph: the Fifteenth Part of` 1) TIMES 15 EQUALS 1
-- What it is given for: the two things the text names, in its words.
#ASSERT `first paragraph: what the Fifteenth Part is given for` EQUALS LIST "this our Gift and Grant of these Liberties", "other contained in our Charter of Liberties of our Forest"

§§ `First paragraph: the promise made "on the other part"`

-- It is granted "unto them": the classes who gave. Same nine; the rest are not named.
#ASSERT `first paragraph: the promise is granted unto` `an Archbishop` EQUALS `covered by the text`
#ASSERT `first paragraph: the promise is granted unto` `a Bishop` EQUALS `covered by the text`
#ASSERT `first paragraph: the promise is granted unto` `an Abbot` EQUALS `covered by the text`
#ASSERT `first paragraph: the promise is granted unto` `a Prior` EQUALS `covered by the text`
#ASSERT `first paragraph: the promise is granted unto` `an Earl` EQUALS `covered by the text`
#ASSERT `first paragraph: the promise is granted unto` `a Baron` EQUALS `covered by the text`
#ASSERT `first paragraph: the promise is granted unto` `a Freeman of the Realm` EQUALS `not covered by the text`
#ASSERT `first paragraph: the promise is granted unto` `a Templar` EQUALS `not covered by the text`
#ASSERT `first paragraph: the promise is granted unto` `a Hospitaller` EQUALS `not covered by the text`
#ASSERT `first paragraph: the promise is granted unto` `a Knight` EQUALS `covered by the text`
#ASSERT `first paragraph: the promise is granted unto` `a Freeholder` EQUALS `covered by the text`
#ASSERT `first paragraph: the promise is granted unto` `another Subject` EQUALS `covered by the text`
#ASSERT `first paragraph: the promise is granted unto` `another Person` EQUALS `not covered by the text`
-- Neither We nor our Heirs shall procure or do any thing whereby the Liberties are infringed or broken.
-- Arguments: the party; the thing procured or done infringes or breaks the Liberties.
#ASSERT `first paragraph: the King and his Heirs shall not procure or do` `the King` TRUE EQUALS `forbidden by the text`
#ASSERT `first paragraph: the King and his Heirs shall not procure or do` `an Heir of the King` TRUE EQUALS `forbidden by the text`
#ASSERT `first paragraph: the King and his Heirs shall not procure or do` `the King` FALSE EQUALS `not covered by the text`
#ASSERT `first paragraph: the King and his Heirs shall not procure or do` `an Heir of the King` FALSE EQUALS `not covered by the text`
-- A Man of the Realm is not named by this promise.
#ASSERT `first paragraph: the King and his Heirs shall not procure or do` `a Man of the Realm` TRUE EQUALS `not covered by the text`

-- expect: BREACHED
#TRACE `first paragraph: neither the King nor his Heirs shall procure an infringement` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the King` DOES `procure or do a thing whereby the Liberties are infringed or broken` AT 3
-- expect: BREACHED
#TRACE `first paragraph: neither the King nor his Heirs shall procure an infringement` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `an Heir of the King` DOES `procure or do a thing whereby the Liberties are infringed or broken` AT 3
-- Observing is not procuring an infringement: the prohibition stands.
-- expect: STANDING
#TRACE `first paragraph: neither the King nor his Heirs shall procure an infringement` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the King` DOES `observe the Customs and Liberties` AT 3
-- expect: STANDING
#TRACE `first paragraph: neither the King nor his Heirs shall procure an infringement` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 100000)

§§ `First paragraph: a thing procured contrary to the premises`

-- Arguments: it was procured by any person; it is contrary to the premises.
#ASSERT `first paragraph: a thing procured` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `of no force nor effect`
-- The condition is "if any thing be procured by any person contrary to the premises". When it fails, the text does not make the thing void.
-- RECONCILED 2026-10-30: was `#ASSERT `first paragraph: a thing procured` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `not covered by the first unnumbered paragraph``
#ASSERT `first paragraph: a thing procured` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `not made void by the first unnumbered paragraph`
-- RECONCILED 2026-10-30: was `#ASSERT `first paragraph: a thing procured` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `not covered by the first unnumbered paragraph``
#ASSERT `first paragraph: a thing procured` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `not made void by the first unnumbered paragraph`
-- RECONCILED 2026-10-30: was `#ASSERT `first paragraph: a thing procured` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not covered by the first unnumbered paragraph``
#ASSERT `first paragraph: a thing procured` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not made void by the first unnumbered paragraph`

§§ `Second paragraph: ratified, confirmed, made strong, renewed`

#ASSERT `second paragraph: what is confirmed, made strong and renewed` `the grant of the Liberties to the classes of preamble paragraph 2` EQUALS `confirmed and made strong for the King and his Heirs perpetually, and renewed`
#ASSERT `second paragraph: what is confirmed, made strong and renewed` `the grant of the Liberties to the Freemen of chapter 1` EQUALS `confirmed and made strong for the King and his Heirs perpetually, and renewed`
#ASSERT `second paragraph: what is confirmed, made strong and renewed` `the gift of the Fifteenth Part of Moveables` EQUALS `confirmed and made strong for the King and his Heirs perpetually, and renewed`
#ASSERT `second paragraph: what is confirmed, made strong and renewed` `the grant that neither We nor our Heirs shall procure an infringement` EQUALS `confirmed and made strong for the King and his Heirs perpetually, and renewed`
#ASSERT `second paragraph: what is confirmed, made strong and renewed` `a gift or grant this text does not show` EQUALS `not covered by the second unnumbered paragraph`

§§ `Second paragraph: "shall be stedfastly, firmly, and inviolably observed"`

#ASSERT `second paragraph: the Charter and its Articles shall be observed for ever` TRUE EQUALS `covered by the text`
#ASSERT `second paragraph: the Charter and its Articles shall be observed for ever` FALSE EQUALS `not covered by the text`
-- The duty is passive: the text names no one to observe.
#ASSERT `second paragraph: the party the text names to observe` EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Second paragraph: an Article that hath not been kept`

-- Arguments: it is an Article of the same Charter; it hath hitherto been kept.
#ASSERT `second paragraph: an Article that hath not been kept` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `commanded to be firmly observed from henceforth`
#ASSERT `second paragraph: an Article that hath not been kept` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `not commanded by the final clause`
#ASSERT `second paragraph: an Article that hath not been kept` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not commanded by the final clause`
#ASSERT `second paragraph: an Article that hath not been kept` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `not commanded by the final clause`

§§ `Third paragraph: the attestation, as the text gives it`

#ASSERT `third paragraph: the attestation, as the text gives it` EQUALS "In Witness whereof We have caused these our Letters Patents to be made. T. Edward our son at Westminster, the twenty-eighth day of March in the twenty-eighth year of our Reign."
